<p>The final vote actually originally had E-5 directly blaming E-2 in the final vote, but some people found that to be too abrasive. Better to put it back?</p>
<p>Your second point is <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">left as an exercise for the student</span> relies very much on headcanon - depending on your interpretation, the Ethics Committee is the very tippy-top of the Foundation pyramid. Even the O5 have to respect their rulings. What kind of protections do you have in place to prevent that power from being influenced by the outside? Draconian, I'm sure.</p>
<p>Are E-1 through -5 even dumb? They may just have different priorities. E-4 is reasonably sane. E-1 and -3 are just ideological purists with no conscience - E-2 tries to fit in with this category but falters when his own countrymen are on the line, but he's crafty - he knows E-4 and E-5 will vote aye, because they're humanitarian-leaning. E-5 is grossly offended by this - it's my intepretation that E-5 would have voted Aye if E-4 or himself brought it up first. E-5 voting nay is purely a spite vote against E-2, and a message to say &quot;We're even now&quot;, written with thousands of bodies. No one has any leverage against any EC member, except each other.</p>

