<p>I am keen to say that this falls utterly flat for me. The dilemma and the anomaly feel like two separate affairs, and I am puzzled as to how they are connected. The dilemma proposed feels generically tied to any war or major conflict since the 20th century, making it less unique than what it seems to be.</p>
<p>And you have to tie Nanjing to this. It is truly unnecessary to the article, other than perhaps making this dilemma grander in scale. Perhaps that idea can be explored, but that should be in another place. As it is, Nanjing is a sideshow while the main bulk of the article remains waddling in itself.</p>
